# ROVEXO MOBILE FIRST ABSOLUTE ENGINEERING LAW v1.0

**STATUS: OWNER APPROVED · PERMANENT · EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY · NO EXCEPTIONS**

SSOT: `lib/mobile-first/mobile-first-absolute-law-v1.ts`

## Absolute

ROVEXO is a **100% MOBILE FIRST MARKETPLACE**.

**Mobile = reference platform.**  
**Desktop = required compatibility, SECONDARY priority.**

```
Desktop PASS + Mobile FAIL = FAIL
until Mobile is corrected.
```

## Platform priority

1. iPhone Safari (**PRIMARY REFERENCE**)  
2. iPhone Chrome  
3. Android Chrome  
4. Samsung Internet  
5. PWA  
6. iPad Safari  
7. Desktop Chrome  
8. Desktop Edge  
9. Desktop Safari  
10. Desktop Firefox  

## Incomplete / not certified

- Works ONLY on Desktop → **NOT COMPLETE**  
- Works ONLY on Windows → **NOT CERTIFIED**  
- Must work **100% on Mobile first**

## Every new module must verify

Touch · Viewport · Safe Area · Dynamic Toolbar · Keyboard · **visualViewport** · Orientation · HEIC · Camera · Gallery · Upload · Scroll · Swipe · Sticky · Bottom Navigation · PWA · Offline Restore · Session Restore · Cookies · SameSite · Storage · IndexedDB · localStorage · Background Restore · Memory · Performance · Battery

## Every bug

Ask first: **Can this happen ONLY on Mobile?**  
If YES → investigate **Mobile FIRST**. Desktop secondary.

## Every audit

Classify: Desktop · Mobile · Desktop + Mobile  
Never certify Desktop only.

## Owner certification

No module may receive **PASS + FREEZE** until **Mobile Certification** passes.

Mandatory Mobile Certification: iPhone Safari · iPhone Chrome · Android Chrome · Samsung Internet · PWA · Landscape · Portrait · Keyboard Open/Closed · Low Network · 4G · Wi-Fi · Image Upload · Camera · Gallery

## Identity

Mobile and Desktop behaviour must be **identical**, unless Owner explicitly approves platform-specific behaviour.

## Cursor must never

- Treat Desktop / Windows as the reference  
- Claim PASS / FREEZE / CERTIFY without Mobile Certification  
- Skip visualViewport / safe-area / keyboard / HEIC / PWA on new work  
- Prefer Desktop fixes when the defect is Mobile-only  
